<issue_description>
# `socketfromfd` fails on SmartOS (SunOS) due to missing `getsockopt` symbol

## Description

I have encountered an issue when using the `gunicorn.socketfromfd` module on SmartOS (SunOS). The module currently uses `ctypes` to load the `getsockopt` function from the system's `libc`.

However, on SmartOS (SunOS), the `getsockopt` symbol is not exposed in the library as expected by the current implementation. Instead, the functionality is available via the symbol `_so_getsockopt`.

Because the code unconditionally attempts to access `libc.getsockopt`, it fails on this platform. The implementation needs to be adjusted to detect the operating system and bind to the correct symbol (`_so_getsockopt`) when running on SunOS.
</issue_description>

